+### `removeWhere(predicate)` -> `int`
+
+Remove every entry for which `predicate(value, index)` returns a truthy value. Entries are visited once from the front of the queue to the back, and `index` is the zero-based index from before filtering. Returns the number of removed entries. The predicate must be a function; if it throws, the queue is left unchanged.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.removeWhere(function (value, index) {
+  return value % 2 === 0;
+}); // 2
+denque.toArray(); // [1,3]
+```
+
+
+
